# Deploying with Docker

This repo ships generated Docker artifacts: `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`,
`docker-compose.yml`.

## VPS quickstart

On a fresh Debian or Ubuntu VPS:

1. Install Docker (engine plus the Compose plugin):

   ```sh
   curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh
   ```

2. Get this repository onto the server — `git clone`, or `rsync -a` from your
   machine.

3. No environment variables were detected — nothing to configure. If the app
   later needs configuration, add `env_file: .env` to the app service in
   `docker-compose.yml`.

4. Build and start everything:

   ```sh
   docker compose up -d --build
   ```

5. Check status and logs:

   ```sh
   docker compose ps
   docker compose logs -f app
   ```

## Process notes

The `app` service publishes port 3000. For a public deployment put a
reverse proxy in front for TLS and routing. [Caddy](https://caddyserver.com)
is the lowest-effort option — a two-line Caddyfile is enough:

```caddy
app.example.com {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3000
}
```
## Updating

Redeploy after pulling new code with:

```sh
docker compose up -d --build
```
